    "## Logistic Regression"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce6ef350",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ce6ef350"
   },
   "source": [
    "Create a binary target: `Expensive` = 1 if a house's price is above the median, else 0."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8269d91f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.975430Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.975373Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.978421Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.978091Z"
    },
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 206
    },
    "id": "8269d91f",
    "outputId": "a35b18f5-d0ec-4986-b310-1c2af2529878"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['Expensive'] = (df['SalePrice'] > df['SalePrice'].median()).astype(int)\n",
    "df[['SalePrice', 'Expensive']].head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c5edf1bd",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "c5edf1bd"
   },
   "source": [
    "### From Scratch (single feature: GrLivArea)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e273d4cd",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "e273d4cd"
   },
   "source": [
    "Standardize `GrLivArea` again and define the sigmoid function, which squeezes any number into a 0\u20131 probability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9b58f046",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.979034Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.978959Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.980815Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.980480Z"
    },
    "id": "9b58f046"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x = df['GrLivArea'].values\n",
    "y = df['Expensive'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "x_norm = (x - x.mean()) / x.std()\n",
    "\n",
    "def sigmoid(z):\n",
    "    return 1 / (1 + np.exp(-z))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "287db74f",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "287db74f"
   },
   "source": [
    "Train with gradient descent \u2014 same update rule as linear regression, but `h(x)` is now passed through the sigmoid."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "aaced9c7",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.981388Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.981336Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.988911Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.988543Z"
    },
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "aaced9c7",
    "outputId": "c03e2b9b-4bb2-4cb9-91e0-5f8f96bb0513"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "m = len(y)\n",
    "theta0, theta1 = 0.0, 0.0\n",
    "alpha = 0.1\n",
    "iterations = 1000\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(iterations):\n",
    "    z = theta0 + theta1 * x_norm\n",
    "    h = sigmoid(z)\n",
    "    error = h - y\n",
    "    theta0 -= alpha * (1/m) * np.sum(error)\n",
    "    theta1 -= alpha * (1/m) * np.sum(error * x_norm)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"theta0:\", theta0)\n",
    "print(\"theta1:\", theta1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8b09d192",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "8b09d192"
   },
   "source": [
    "Plot the data points (0 = not expensive, 1 = expensive) with the fitted sigmoid curve \u2014 the logistic-regression equivalent of the best-fit line. `x` is sorted first so the curve draws smoothly left to right."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e02a497d",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.989497Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.989446Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-25T05:59:32.022089Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-25T05:59:32.021645Z"
    },
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 472
    },
    "id": "e02a497d",
    "outputId": "dfa1ae4c-918c-4bbc-d6ab-045935756048"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x_sorted = np.sort(x)\n",
    "x_sorted_norm = (x_sorted - x.mean()) / x.std()\n",
    "y_curve = sigmoid(theta0 + theta1 * x_sorted_norm)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.scatter(x, y, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "plt.plot(x_sorted, y_curve, color='red')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"GrLivArea\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Expensive (0/1)\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Logistic Regression From Scratch\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
